{"ts": "2026-07-06T02:09:21.259018+00:00", "run_id": "20260706T020916Z_af6cff6d", "event": "tool_result", "turn": 3, "tool_call_id": "call_f632ca69eb2840ca86c1b06bd0c3__thought__", "name": "get_template", "result": "{\n  \"name\": \"scaling_depth\",\n  \"content\": \"meta:\\n  name: \\\"Scaling depth: is the 1M->10M kink a boundary or just acceleration?\\\"\\n  description: >\\n    find_kink.py on the published capsules flags a consistent per-decade slowdown\\n    spike at the 1M->10M interval across duckdb, quack, and quack_pushdown\\n    (~1.7x/decade up to 1M, then ~6-11x). This experiment tests what that kink is.\\n    Two fixes over the original 4-point matrix: add 10K to make the low decades\\n    evenly spaced (a clean per-decade baseline), and add 100M as a point ABOVE the\\n    kink \\u2014 the decisive one. If per-decade settles back after 10M, the kink is a\\n    localized cache-hierarchy boundary; if it keeps climbing, it is monotonic\\n    acceleration, not a kink. analytical_wall is a 12-group aggregation, so its\\n    operator memory does NOT scale with N \\u2014 this isolates scan/cache scaling, and\\n    memory_limit is deliberately NOT swept here (see memory_spill_probe.yaml for\\n    the operator-memory question). Cold cache, replication 5.\\n    Note: attach (quack) and postgres at 100M may be very slow or DNF \\u2014 that is\\n    recorded as data, not treated as failure.\\n\\ndataset:\\n  source: sql_benchmarks.plugins.data_sources.declarative_gen\\n  tables:\\n    analytical_data:\\n      rows: rows\\n      columns:\\n        - name: id\\n          provider: sequence\\n          primary_key: true\\n        - name: region\\n          provider: choice\\n          options: [\\\"North\\\", \\\"South\\\", \\\"East\\\", \\\"West\\\"]\\n        - name: category\\n          provider: choice\\n          options: [\\\"A\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"C\\\"]\\n        - name: price\\n          provider: random_float\\n          min_value: 10.0\\n          max_value: 500.0\\n        - name: quantity\\n          provider: random_int\\n          min_value: 1\\n          max_value: 100\\n        - name: discount\\n          provider: random_float\\n          min_value: 0.0\\n          max_value: 0.30\\n\\ndefinitions:\\n  rows:\\n    tiny:   1_000\\n    xs:     10_000\\n    small:  100_000\\n    medium: 1_000_000\\n    large:  10_000_000\\n    xlarge: 100_000_000\\n\\nexecution:\\n  test_suite: analytical_wall\\n  engines:\\n    - duckdb\\n    - quack\\n    - quack_pushdown\\n    - postgres\\n  replication: 5\\n  matrix:\\n    rows:\\n      - tiny\\n      - xs\\n      - small\\n      - medium\\n      - large\\n      - xlarge\\n\",\n  \"path\": \"queue/scaling_depth.yaml\"\n}", "result_len": 2383, "error_reason": null}
